			"date": "2024-02-26T19:41:36.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@mikeneu\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>mikeneu</span></a></span> <br>Neat! I think it could benefit from a toggle to make it a static transcript, without the interactivity, so people can read it without the timecodes or button semantics while using a screen reader or any text-to-speech tech.</p><p>The toggle control could do something like add/remove a 'static' class on the custom element and make the click handler inactive.</p><p>```CSS<br>youtube-deep-link.static [data-offset] button {<br>    display: none;<br>}<br>```</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
